  "honest_findings": [
    "JAMMER SITING IS THE DOMINANT VARIABLE, AND IT IS MEASURED. Over 128 real campus grid points a 23 dBm jammer denies (11 dB SINR) between 47.2% and 100.0% of the campus (median 64.9%), against an unjammed baseline of 47.2%. The worst site is [160.449, 56.8308, 1.5] m, 52 m from the BS; the best is [-203.551, -156.169, 1.5] m at 452 m. Outage correlates with the jammer's measured gain to the BS (Pearson r=0.959) more tightly than with its straight-line distance to the BS (r=-0.746). Distance is a usable proxy but the ray-traced gain field is the thing: siting rules should be written against measured propagation, not a radius on a map.",
    "SUBBAND ESCAPE IS WORTH LESS THAN IT SOUNDS, AND WE MEASURED HOW MUCH. At the representative (median-outage) real jammer site, subband selection is worth 2.010 dB of mean SINR over a fixed subband \u2014 but making that selection *jamming-aware* rather than just best-gain adds only 0.097 dB (0.113 dB over the 2164 receivers the un-jammed cell can actually serve), even though 1266 of 4096 receivers do change which subband is optimal. The reason is measurable in the data: the jammer's interference is common to every victim and its ray-traced per-subband profile is only a few dB wide, so the victim's own gain variation dominates the choice. Anyone selling jamming-aware DSA as a large win on this geometry is overselling.",
    "LEGALITY IS INDEPENDENT OF THE ATTACK. At all three real jammer sites, every one of 4096 escape decisions was pushed through the Shield with a deliberately over-limit 44 dBm request; 4096 were projected and 0 illegal carriers in total reached the air interface. A jammer can take the throughput; it cannot make the rApp emit outside its licence.",
    "BARRAGE (broadband AWGN) jammer: both receivers degrade together as JSR rises (at the measured p90 JSR=25.955 dB neural SER 0.933, LMMSE SER 0.932). The Shield CANNOT fix a noisier channel \u2014 it only routes between receivers \u2014 so the effective SER (0.933) tracks the better receiver but is still degraded. This is the Shield's stated limitation.",
    "PARTIAL-BAND / PULSED / SINGLE-TONE jammers degrade SER monotonically with JSR as well; partial-band severity also rises with the jammed fraction. The Shield still only routes \u2014 it cannot denoise.",
    "IMPERFECT CSI on the measured channel: at sigma_est=0.4, neural SER 0.346 vs LMMSE SER 0.356 \u2014 the LMMSE equaliser degrades MORE (its conj(\u0124)/(|\u0124|\u00b2+N0) weights are directly corrupted by the CSI error)."
  ],
